# Night View UI (Report-O-Matic)

Night mode is **`html[data-rom-theme="night"]`**, set by `DisplayModeSwitcher` / `UiLanguageProvider` — **not** Tailwind `dark:`.

Global overrides live in **`app/src/app/globals.css`**. New UI must use class patterns that those rules already remap, or extend `globals.css` in the same file when introducing new surface utilities.

## Prefer these patterns (day + night safe)

| Use | Avoid (often invisible at night) |
|-----|----------------------------------|
| `bg-white`, `bg-emerald-50`, `bg-emerald-50/70` | `bg-zinc-50/40`, `bg-zinc-50/90`, opaque zinc panels |
| `border-emerald-200` | `border-emerald-300/80` alone without a globals rule |
| `text-zinc-900`, `text-zinc-700`, `text-zinc-500` | Hard-coded `#000`, inline `style={{ color }}` |
| `bg-emerald-800` + `text-white` for primary buttons | `bg-zinc-900` on navy shell (prefer emerald CTA) |
| `text-amber-800` on panels (globals darkens amber bg) | Pale amber bg + light amber text only |

## Before merging UI work

1. Mentally check the block against **`globals.css`** `html[data-rom-theme="night"]` selectors (`bg-white`, `bg-emerald-50`, `text-zinc-*`, `border-emerald-200`, etc.).
2. If you need a new Tailwind combo (e.g. new opacity suffix or ring colour), add a matching **`[class*="…"]`** night rule in `globals.css` — do not rely on day-only colours.
3. Smoke-test in the app: **Display → Night View** on dashboard Subjects/Classes and any new screen.

## Reference

- Theme state: `app/src/components/i18n/UiLanguageProvider.tsx` (`displayTheme`, `data-rom-theme`).
- Subjects grade-title editor: `app/src/components/reports/TenantClassesPanel.tsx` (`view="subjects"`).

## UI strings (i18n)

- Use `t("…")` only — no hardcoded user-facing English in components.
- New keys: add to **EN**, **FR**, and **ES** in `app/src/lib/i18n/uiStrings.ts`; mirror in `localeUiFill.ts` (`UI_FILL_FR` / `UI_FILL_ES`) when the key lives only in the EN block; add **de / it / pt** in `localeExtra.ts` for full secondary-locale coverage.
- Run `node app/scripts/check-ui-i18n-keys.mjs` after adding keys.
